From: j7 console and speed
Subject: a5xelte fb: initialize the console-mute flag so a5fb_noconsole actually mutes

The panel kept the boot log at the bottom after the first swap even with a5fb_noconsole=1.
AppleCLCD::present() mutes the console in a "first swap" block guarded by fConsolePaused, but that
member is never initialized: the IOKit object is not zero-filled and there is no constructor for it,
so a first swap that found it non-zero skipped the whole block (mute, and the panel clear with it)
for the rest of the boot.  Set the flag (and the other uninitialized state the vsync path reads)
explicitly in start(), and log the mute so the next boot log says whether it ran.

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
index 2f969ac..f9f58c7 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetFramebuffer.cpp
@@ -293,6 +293,13 @@ AppleCLCD::start(IOService *provider)
 #else
 	fFlushTicks = (hz == 0 || hz >= 60) ? 1 : 60 / hz;
 #endif
+	/* The IOKit object is not zero-filled and none of these are constructor-initialized.  A
+	 * fConsolePaused that happened to read true skipped the console mute for the whole boot, which
+	 * is why the panel kept the boot log at the bottom after a5fb_noconsole=1. */
+	fConsolePaused = false;
+	fDirty = false;
+	fPowerOff = false;
+	fFadeStep = 0;
 #if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_HEROLTE)
 	sweet_fb_copy_init();
 #endif
@@ -642,6 +649,7 @@ AppleCLCD::present(const uint8_t *rec)
 			/* Not PE_initialize_console(kPEDisableScreen): its console switch
 			 * writes the read-only-late cons_ops_index and panics. */
 			sweet_console_muted = 1;
+			IOLog("A5XELTE FB: console muted (a5fb_noconsole), panel cleared\n");
 			/* Whatever the console drew before this first swap stays on screen wherever the GUI
 			 * does not draw (boot log lines at the bottom, junk at the top): start from black.
 			 * fPixels is the physical map of the whole panel, scaledCopy() writes all of it too. */
